<title>BELGIUM: ERM membership &quot;a moot point&quot; - Dutch Zalm.</title>
<headline>ERM membership &quot;a moot point&quot; - Dutch Zalm.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Finance Minister Gerrit Zalm on Monday said participation in Europe's exchange rate mechanism as a condition for joining the single currency was subject to interpretation.</p>
<p>Responding to questions over whether Britain must rejoin the ERM should it want to participate in a single currency, Zalm said &quot;There is some difference of interpretation among lawyers. That's a moot point, and is subject to interpretation.&quot;</p>
<p>Zalm noted that what was important in assessing currency stability was whether a country had devalued its currency in the run-up to monetary union.</p>
<p>Earlier Britain's chancellor of the exchequer Gordon Brown said he did not believe participation in the ERM was a pre-condition for joining the single currency. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
